// @run
// @log 5
// @log 2
// @log 7
// The annotation IS the cell under test here, so its redundancy hints are declared
// rather than removed — un-annotating the binding is a DIFFERENT cell with a different
// root (`variant-fieldset-twin-anon-shape-floor.vl`), as the floor's own notes record.
// That sibling's floor has since lifted too (D244 gave the UN-annotated global the same
// kind-8 variant cell this annotated one already had), so it is `@run` now; the two roots
// stay distinct — this one is `letAnnVariantIdx`'s annotated rung, that one is
// `objLitVariantIdxNoStructRow`'s field-set rung under a no-struct-row precondition.
// @hint redundant type annotation: `g` is inferred as `{p: i32}`
// @hint redundant type annotation: `o` is inferred as `{p: i32}`
// @hint redundant type annotation: `gc` is inferred as `Outer`
// THE FLOOR IS LIFTED. This file was an `@emit-error ref valtype with no interned shape` pin
// with the instruction "flip it when the floor lifts"; it is flipped, and the pin is now the
// behaviour rather than the refusal.
//
// A module GLOBAL annotated with a union-VARIANT type name. `types/variant-as-value.vl` pins a
// variant type as a first-class value in every OTHER position — local, param, return, argument,
// array element — so this was the one position that pin did not reach, and the gap was the
// position, not the feature.
//
// THE MECHANISM, as the floor recorded it: `buildLocals` has a `variant` rung (`letIsVariant` →
// kind 8, the bare variant struct ref) ahead of its `letIsUnion`/`letIsStruct` rungs.
// `globalCellKind`, whose own header says it mirrors that ladder, had no such rung — so the
// annotation fell to `letIsStruct`, `globalCellStructIdx` asked `structIndexOfLet`, and a
// variant's `TypeDecl` is deliberately absent from the struct table (`collectS` skips it; the
// variant table owns it). Index -1 then tripped `fbValtypeNullable`'s out-of-bounds guard.
//
// THE FIX IS THE ONE THE FLOOR NAMED, and it reuses #1803's four pieces rather than adding a
// rep: `globalCellKind`'s annotated arm grew the `variant` rung in the same slot the local
// ladder puts it (before `letIsUnion`/`letIsStruct`), `globalCellStructIdx`'s annotated arm
// answers `letAnnVariantIdx` before falling to `structIndexOfLet`, and both global-init paths
// — the constexpr one in the global section and the non-const one in the start fn — seed
// `pendingVariantIdx` beside the `pendingStructIdx` they already seeded. `globalKind`'s variant
// arm, `fbRefNullForKind`'s `uVarHeap` zero-init and `exprVariantIndex`'s module-global leg all
// shipped with the UN-ANNOTATED half in #1803 and needed no change.
//
// The floor's own measured cells, kept because they are what makes this a position gap:
//   - the identical binding as a LOCAL inside a function lowered and printed even then —
//     STORAGE CLASS WAS THE AXIS;
//   - as a function PARAM it lowered;
//   - a struct|struct union (`Outer | Other`) floored exactly as this struct|scalar one did,
//     so union MIXEDNESS was not the axis;
//   - a NESTED field (`{p: Inner}`) as a local lowered, so nesting was not the axis either;
//   - un-annotating the binding CHANGED the message to `field access but no struct type
//     declared` — a separate floor with a separate root
//     (`variant-fieldset-twin-anon-shape-floor.vl`). That floor has since lifted (D244);
//     the two roots were and remain distinct, and the sibling is `@run` today.
type Outer = { p: i32 }
type U = Outer | i32

const g: Outer = { p: 5 }
print(g.p)

// The position the floor blocked in practice: build at the ARM type, then widen into the
// union. Both spellings of the widen — a binding and an argument — go through this cell.
type Rect = { w: f64 }
type Shape = Outer | Rect
const o: Outer = { p: 2 }
const sh: Shape = o
if sh is Outer { print(sh.p) }

// A NON-CONST initializer takes the start-fn path, which seeds the same variant context.
function mk(): Outer { return { p: 7 } }
const gc: Outer = mk()
print(gc.p)
